c('Data are2,4,6,8. Find the mean,median,and MAD. Duplicate every observation so the new data contain eight values. Predict and verify which of the three measures changes.','Bothsetsmean5,median5,MAD2;nonechanges.','The originaltotal20over4 gives5,andmiddlepair4,6 gives5. Distances3,1,1,3 average2. Duplicating doubles both the total andcount,and also both the totaldistance andcount;each ratio is unchanged. The newmiddlepair remains4,6.','S-MAD','F(sum([2,4,6,8]),4)==F(sum([2,2,4,4,6,6,8,8]),8)==5 and statistics.median([2,4,6,8])==statistics.median([2,2,4,4,6,6,8,8])==5 and F(sum(abs(x-5) for x in [2,4,6,8]),4)==F(sum(abs(x-5) for x in [2,2,4,4,6,6,8,8]),8)==2','What happens to numerator anddenominator when every observation is duplicated?','Write total/count and totaldistance/count.','Two data rows,second containing eachfirst-rowvalue twice.'),
